# cauce behind Caddy — TLS termination + reverse proxy.
#
#   caddy run --config contrib/Caddyfile
#
# DOMAIN is read from the environment (`DOMAIN=search.example.com`),
# falling back to localhost for a quick check. Set
# `rate_limit.trust_proxy_headers = true` in /etc/cauce/config.toml —
# Caddy forwards X-Forwarded-For and without it every client lands in
# the same per-IP bucket. No extra cache policy is needed here: cauce
# stamps `Cache-Control` itself (`[edge]`); Caddy honours it.
#
# For a *private* instance drop this file entirely — cloudflared
# (`cloudflared tunnel --url http://127.0.0.1:4479`) or Tailscale keeps
# the box unexposed, which is the reference setup in docs/deploy/.

{$DOMAIN:localhost} {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:4479
	encode zstd gzip
}
